[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759740967","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104705#issuecomment-2759740967","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104705","id":2759740967,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kfk4n","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-27T23:01:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T23:01:56Z","body":"This is to be expected and is documented, there's no type checking so the implicit conversion can't happen, this is something that needs to be done explicitly\n\nI'd say the thing to do is perhaps document this even more clearly and make it clear that no conersions at all are done, not just that no checking is done","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759740967/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759932649","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104705#issuecomment-2759932649","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104705","id":2759932649,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kgTrp","user":{"login":"shoonee","id":55113941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTEzOTQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55113941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee","html_url":"https://github.com/shoonee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T01:21:10Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T01:21:10Z","body":"Is there a purpose to allowing this undefined behavior though, as opposed to coercing types or preventing mismatched types? Tweens will implicitly cast between `float` and `int`, or fail if a value of an improper type is given.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759932649/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2762339571","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104705#issuecomment-2762339571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104705","id":2762339571,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kpfTz","user":{"login":"shoonee","id":55113941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTEzOTQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55113941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee","html_url":"https://github.com/shoonee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T20:05:32Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T20:05:32Z","body":"After some further investigating, it seems that cases where multiple GDScript types correspond to a single shader type would make type checking or type conversions a bit complicated. I would propose the following changes (in order of importance):\n\n1. Add the same note about needing the types to match from the [shading language docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html#setting-uniforms-from-code) to the [ShaderMaterial docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_shadermaterial.html#class-shadermaterial-method-set-shader-parameter).\n2. Let `set_shader_parameter()` implicity convert between `int` and `float`, the same way `Tween` does.\n3. Add some type checking to `set_shader_parameter()` and warn about incompatible types. I could go a couple different ways on choosing which types are incompatible, like letting you truncate `Vector4` to `Vector3`, or converting between `Vector3i` and `Vector3`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2762339571/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3446813163","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104705#issuecomment-3446813163","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104705","id":3446813163,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NcjHr","user":{"login":"Lindbrum","id":26764132,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzY0MTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26764132?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum","html_url":"https://github.com/Lindbrum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lindbrum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-25T14:58:07Z","updated_at":"2025-10-25T14:58:07Z","body":"I want to add that the very same happens with `set_instance_shader_parameter()`. It did drive me crazy yesterday because my shader flat out stopped working without any warning/error.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3446813163/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448675543","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104705#issuecomment-3448675543","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104705","id":3448675543,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NjpzX","user":{"login":"shoonee","id":55113941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTEzOTQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55113941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee","html_url":"https://github.com/shoonee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoonee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-26T16:30:27Z","updated_at":"2025-10-26T16:30:27Z","body":"> I want to add that the very same happens with `set_instance_shader_parameter()`. It did drive me crazy yesterday because my shader flat out stopped working without any warning/error.\n\nI do have an open PR, but at the moment it wouldn't cover that use case. The same check could be added to `set_instance_shader_parameter()` too. There's probably a cleaner way to implicitly convert types to cover all + future use cases involving shader parameters, but I'm not sure where in the code base shaders apply the parameters.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448675543/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]